#!/bin/busybox sh
# Boot initramfs for SteamOS-ARM-SM8650. Mounts the root, leaves the kernel
# log from this boot in bootlog.txt on the FAT boot partition (the only way
# to diagnose a black screen without a serial console), then switch_roots.
# konkr.bootlog_wait=N on the cmdline adds N extra 4-second log snapshots
# before booting (debugging display/driver bring-up).
#
# Root: root=PARTLABEL=<name> (internal UFS install: STORAGE, boot log on
# ROCKNIX); anything else is the microSD image (p1 boot, p2 root).
/bin/busybox --install -s /bin
export PATH=/bin
mount -t devtmpfs dev /dev
mount -t proc proc /proc
mount -t sysfs sys /sys
mkdir -p /boot /newroot

extra=0
rootarg=""
for arg in $(cat /proc/cmdline); do
  case "$arg" in
    konkr.bootlog_wait=*) extra="${arg#*=}" ;;
    root=*) rootarg="${arg#root=}" ;;
  esac
done

# /dev node of the partition with GPT name $1, if present.
by_partlabel() {
  for u in /sys/class/block/*/uevent; do
    if grep -qx "PARTNAME=$1" "$u"; then
      d="${u%/uevent}"
      echo "/dev/${d##*/}"
      return 0
    fi
  done
  return 1
}

bootdev=""
rootdev=""
case "$rootarg" in
  PARTLABEL=*)
    # UFS comes up a few seconds into boot.
    for i in $(seq 1 60); do
      rootdev="$(by_partlabel "${rootarg#PARTLABEL=}")" && break
      sleep 0.5
    done
    bootdev="$(by_partlabel ROCKNIX)"
    ;;
  *)
    for i in $(seq 1 60); do
      for p in /sys/class/block/mmcblk*p1; do
        [ -e "$p" ] && bootdev="/dev/$(basename "$p")" && break 2
      done
      sleep 0.5
    done
    [ -n "$bootdev" ] && rootdev="${bootdev%p1}p2"
    ;;
esac

snap() {
  [ -n "$bootdev" ] || return
  {
    echo "=== $1  uptime $(cat /proc/uptime)"
    echo "--- cmdline"; cat /proc/cmdline
    echo "--- partitions"; cat /proc/partitions
    echo "--- drm"; ls /sys/class/drm 2>&1
    echo "--- dmesg"; dmesg
  } > /boot/bootlog.txt 2>&1
  sync
}

if [ -n "$bootdev" ] && mount -t vfat "$bootdev" /boot; then
  n=0
  while [ "$n" -lt "$extra" ]; do snap "snapshot $n"; sleep 4; n=$((n + 1)); done
fi

if [ -n "$rootdev" ] && mount -t ext4 -o rw "$rootdev" /newroot; then
  if [ -f /newroot/var/lib/konkr-update/pending ]; then
    if ! ( . /konkr-update-recover ); then
      snap "UPDATE RECOVERY FAILED"
      echo "Update recovery failed; system boot stopped to protect the installation"
      exec sh
    fi
  fi
  # SteamOS keeps /etc as an overlay (etc.mount). Mounted by systemd it comes
  # up after systemd has read its units, so anything enabled at runtime (the
  # links in the upper layer, e.g. `systemctl enable sshd`) was ignored on the
  # next boot. Mount it here; systemd then treats etc.mount as already active.
  e=/newroot/var/lib/overlays/etc
  if [ -d "$e/upper" ]; then
    mkdir -p "$e/work"
    mount -t overlay overlay \
      -o "lowerdir=/newroot/etc,upperdir=$e/upper,workdir=$e/work" /newroot/etc \
      || echo "etc overlay mount failed; systemd will retry" >/dev/kmsg
  fi
  snap "root mounted from $rootdev, switch_root"
  umount /boot 2>/dev/null
  exec switch_root /newroot /sbin/init
fi
snap "FAILED to mount root ($rootdev)"
echo "root mount failed; see bootlog.txt on the FAT partition"
exec sh
